vee runtime: POSIX sh and common Unix utilities (including awk, sed, sort,
fold, find, head, tail, cut, and date with +%s support). groff and fmt are optional: the
default formatter falls back to fmt or fold. Perl is required only to run the tests.

Install all six executable commands from bin/ into one directory on PATH:

    mkdir -p "$HOME/bin"
    cp bin/vee bin/veels bin/veecat bin/veefind bin/vee-rebuild bin/vee-publish "$HOME/bin/"
    chmod 755 "$HOME/bin/vee" "$HOME/bin/veels" "$HOME/bin/veecat" "$HOME/bin/veefind" "$HOME/bin/vee-rebuild" "$HOME/bin/vee-publish"
    PATH="$HOME/bin:$PATH"
    export PATH

Alternatively, add the checkout's bin/ directory to PATH. No build step.

Change to your web/Gopher publication directory and run vee. It creates .vee/
and the relevant indexes. EDITOR chooses the editor (default: vi). Configuration
is optional: copy dot.veerc to .veerc in the publication directory if desired.
Use vee -h or README.md for commands and configuration.

The optional vee-publish helper additionally requires rsync and SSH.
